-- title:
--   Supersingular special-fibre points fixed by relative chart automorphisms
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, with $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ and $K_1$ be intermediate fields of $L \subseteq L((q))$ with $K$ the subfield generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of the function field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137) and $K_1$ the subfield generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.x1x0FunctionFieldC ℚ M p`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L142), the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the integral form ratios for $\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p)$, and assume $K_1 \le K$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, compatibly an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ and on $K_1$ over $L$; let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $j \in K$ and $j_1 \in K_1$ be nonzero elements both mapping to the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular invariant in $L((q))$. Write $R =$ `chartAlgFin A K j` and $R_1 =$ `chartAlgFin A K₁ j₁` for the subalgebras of elements integral over $A[j]$, resp. $A[j_1]$, and let $\iota_F : R_1 \to R$ be an $A$-algebra map compatible with the inclusions into $L((q))$. Let $y$ be a point of $\operatorname{Spec} R$ whose prime ideal contains the image of $\varpi$, and assume that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $p$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : R \to \Omega$ with kernel the prime of $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet p Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of $j$-invariants such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that invariant has no nonzero point $P$ with $p \cdot P = 0$. Then for every $A$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $R$ with $\tau(\iota_F r) = \iota_F r$ for all $r \in R_1$, the contraction of the prime of $y$ along $\tau$ equals that prime.
--
--   This is the statement that a supersingular point of the special fibre of the $j$-finite chart of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ over $A$ is fixed by every automorphism of that chart which acts trivially on the chart of $X(\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(p))$; the mechanism behind it is the total ramification of the covering at supersingular points. It feeds the analysis of the supersingular points of the special fibre in [`ModularCurve.XOneP.eq_of_comap_eq_and_forall_exists_sub_mem_of_map_jChartFin_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.eq_of_comap_eq_and_forall_exists_sub_mem_of_map_jChartFin_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel_x1_mul).
